{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793205997,"nonce":"IwPguHNR+4xQARWLaM6Gnis5wk0=","message":"Implementation now shares the main collected-content/ordered app frame pipeline between render_tree and render_tree_with_motion_opt. RenderTree::render_snapshot supplies no entry/exit animation state; the existing walker accepts an optional state and preserves all existing Some-state behavior. No new RenderState or scheduler is constructed. The separate legacy app preparation/dispatch implementation was removed. Cache ownership includes snapshot versus entry/exit-state mode, and snapshot calls release replay batches and promoted textures after dispatch rather than retaining an unused frame cache.\n\nFour new GPU cases pass normally: overlapping canvas/text opacity at .5/0/1/.75/.5 with repeated frames, both text pipeline modes, 1x/4x and DPI1/2; ImageElement and Div-image backgrounds, SVG, StyledText and foreground with brightness/opacity; nested foreground opacity with a parent clip; and interleaved stateless/animated/compositor frames preserving entry-animation values and the original global scheduler spring sentinel. The initial test fixture used a wrong inset field name and then omitted compositor COPY_DST usage; both were corrected before the final matrix.\n\nAll 85 scoped normal tests pass. They include the four new cases, main text clip, foreground RGBA, selected application image/path/affine and multi-canvas clipping sequences, mixed boundaries, cross-stream/effect groups, grouped and styled text, SVG/image groups, named sampling, tree-scope caches and CSS lifecycle. The seven pre-change controls remain green. Logs /private/tmp/blinc-snapshot-final-*.log; global-scheduler sentinel rerun /private/tmp/blinc-snapshot-final-sentinel.log. Scoped app/layout library clippy passes. The four new cases also pass with data textures; capability source was restored byte-for-byte and restored-normal verification is finishing.\n\nCosts/limits: stateless rendering now performs the same group bakes and collected-content preparation as the supported animated path, including glyph preparation and retained image/SVG payloads. This replaces incomplete legacy behavior. Replay CPU batches and promoted GPU textures are released after each snapshot; image/font caches and normal tree paint metadata remain available. Existing texture pool policies are unchanged. The shared pipeline still uses its existing transient frame preparation/cache-clone machinery before cleanup; no timing or peak-memory benchmark is claimed. The RenderTree::render_snapshot API is additive; existing public signatures, GPU/shader/primitive/FFI layouts and StableNodeId are unchanged. Independent-context layout painting and unsupported owner combinations remain in the parent. No broad gates, desktop input, push or publication.","files":null}]}